%USERPROFILE%\.gemini\antigravity-cli\bin\agentapi.bat   -> "C:\Users\PICHAU\AppData\Local\agy\bin\agy.exe" agentapi %*
%USERPROFILE%\.gemini\antigravity-cli\bin\webm_encoder.exe (13 MB)
## `antigravity.cmd` on PATH is the IDE launcher, another product (first facts, #729).

## WSL Ubuntu
$ ls -la ~/.local/bin/agy; ~/.local/bin/agy --version; which agy
-rwxr-xr-x 1 corcino corcino 279462288 Nov 12 07:47 /home/corcino/.local/bin/agy
1.5.6
/home/corcino/.local/bin/agy
$ cat ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/bin/agentapi
#!/bin/sh
exec "/home/corcino/.local/bin/agy.1793217806081684432.old" agentapi "$@"
## The shim still names the pre-update binary, which the updater renamed to .old.

## Install commands (documentation only: https://antigravity.google/docs/getting-started)
Windows (PowerShell): irm https://antigravity.google/cli/install.ps1 | iex
Windows (CMD):        curl -fsSL https://antigravity.google/cli/install.cmd -o install.cmd && install.cmd && del install.cmd
                      default binary location: C:\Users\<username>\AppData\Local\agy\bin
macOS / Linux:        curl -fsSL https://antigravity.google/cli/install.sh | bash
                      default binary location: ~/.local/bin/agy
No Homebrew, npm or winget package is named. The install scripts take --skip-aliases and --skip-path
(https://antigravity.google/docs/install).

$ agy install --help
Usage: agy.exe install [flags]
Configure environment paths and shell settings
Flags:
  --dir           Custom directory target to configure PATH for
  --skip-aliases  Bypasses shell profile alias purging
  --skip-path     Bypasses shell profile PATH appending

## Sign-in for CI (documentation only: https://antigravity.google/docs/install)
Gemini API key: set "modelProvider": "gemini" in ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/settings.json, then export
GEMINI_API_KEY (the variable alone has no effect; .env files are ignored).
Application Default Credentials: gcloud auth application-default login --project <project>, then
AGY_ADC_AUTH=true (optional GOOGLE_CLOUD_QUOTA_PROJECT, GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION).

## Windows stdout encoding (the one model call of this stage, isolated root, Flash)
$ agy --gemini_dir=<tmp> -p "Reply in one line. Start with the exact text: ação ✓ 日本. ..." \
      --model gemini-3.8-flash-low --output-format json --print-timeout 150s </dev/null > win-call.out
exit=0
$ od -c win-call.out | head        (the bytes of "response":"ação ✓ 日本 ...)
0000000   "   r   e   s   p   o   n   s   e   "   :   "   a 303 247 303
0000020 243   o     342 234 223     346 227 245 346 234 254       M   A
## UTF-8 bytes on a pipe, not the console code page (ç = 303 247, ✓ = 342 234 223, 日 = 346 227 245).

